---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About | Usman Ramzan"
  description="Lahore-based CTO and technical advisor. Seven years across Emumba, Unifonic, and Eprecisio, building cloud platforms where downtime is not an option."
>
  <section class="py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl grid-cols-1 gap-12 px-6 md:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="md:col-span-8">
        <h1 class="font-display text-5xl font-medium tracking-tight md:text-7xl">About</h1>
        <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            I'm Usman Ramzan. I live in Lahore, and for the last seven years I have worked on the
            part of software that nobody notices until it breaks: the infrastructure underneath it.
          </p>
          <p>
            The short version of my career. I started at Emumba in 2019 as a DevOps engineer and
            founded their Cloud Center of Excellence, building HIPAA and PCI compliant architectures
            on AWS and Azure. Then Unifonic, a messaging platform sending over ten billion messages a
            year, where I spent three years, ran about three hundred Kubernetes nodes, and led the
            migration of roughly forty applications from AWS to Oracle Cloud. Since September 2025 I
            have been CTO at Eprecisio, where I own the technology strategy for an enterprise
            multi-cloud Kubernetes platform.
          </p>
          <p>
            People ask what a CTO actually does all day. At Eprecisio I pick what we build versus
            buy, keep tenant provisioning fast (it went from eight to ten minutes to about fifty
            seconds), and make sure the platform stays reliable as it grows across twelve cloud
            providers. Alongside that I am fractional CTO to four companies, which mostly means
            turning vague technical anxiety into a ranked list of problems with owners and dates.
          </p>
          <p>
            The thread through all of it: I like infrastructure that is boring, reliable, and honest
            about its costs. Downtime is the most expensive feature anyone can ship, and cost
            surprises are downtime that has not happened yet. I care about compliance for the same
            reason. SOC 2, HIPAA, and GDPR are not trophies; they are the checklist that lets a
            company sell to customers who need proof.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-10">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-medium">Now</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-muted">
            <li>CTO at Eprecisio Technologies</li>
            <li>Fractional CTO to four companies</li>
            <li>
              Building <a href="https://urnlabs.com" class="text-accent underline-offset-4 hover:underline">URN Labs</a>
            </li>
            <li>Writing here occasionally</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="md:col-span-4">
        <!-- TODO: add a real photo slot. Empty bordered 3:4 box until a portrait exists. -->
        <div class="flex aspect-[3/4] w-full items-center justify-center border border-line bg-[#f4f4f2]" aria-hidden="true"><span class="font-mono text-5xl text-[#d4d4d0]">UR</span></div>
        <div class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-8">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-medium">Where I have been</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
            <li>
              <p class="font-medium">Eprecisio Technologies</p>
              <p class="text-muted">CTO, Sep 2025 &rarr; present</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p class="font-medium">Unifonic</p>
              <p class="text-muted">Senior Infrastructure Engineer 2024-2025 &middot; DevOps Engineer 2022-2024</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p class="font-medium">Emumba</p>
              <p class="text-muted">DevOps Engineer 2019-2022</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
